Task: Implement (Green) - PATCH /orders/{id} update endpoint

Summary:
Added OrderStore[F].update(id, quantity, status): F[Option[Order]] to both
backends. In-memory: Ref.modify, replacing the stored order if present (None
otherwise). Postgres: a single UPDATE ... RETURNING item, quantity, status,
created_at, updated_at query (sets updated_at = now()), using .option so a
missing/malformed id cleanly yields None without a separate SELECT round trip.
Order and OrderResponse both gain an updatedAt field (create sets it equal to
createdAt; update bumps it).

Added a tapir PATCH /orders/{id} endpoint (UpdateOrderRequest body: quantity,
status - both required, matching the plan's literal OrderStore.update
signature rather than a field-by-field partial patch) - 200 with the updated
order, or the existing notFoundOutput (404) if the id doesn't exist. Wired into
OrderRoutes.routes and Main's Docs.routes list.

Extended OrderRoutesSuite (success, 404, and logging tests for PATCH, plus
failingStore now implements update) and OrderStorePostgresSuite (update
success/unknown-id/malformed-id tests against real Postgres).

Files changed:
- src/main/scala/orderservice/{Main,OrderRoutes,OrderStore}.scala
- src/test/scala/orderservice/{OrderRoutesSuite,OrderStorePostgresSuite}.scala

Why: Implements this track's FR4 partial-update requirement (spec.md) -
quantity/status changes, with updated_at set on every update.

